  "context": "Expose reusable loaders rather than a lint-specific bulk path: load_item_snapshots(ids) plus lint_item(snapshot, config), so single-item lint, bulk lint, and any future compact projection share one loader.",
  "description": "cli.py:1341-1342 calls tracker.lint (and so get_item) for every id from list_items(), which has no state filter. On BenchBox that is all 2224 items at roughly nine queries each plus the work_needs fan-out: on the order of 20000 statements per invocation, the worst path in the codebase. Bulk-load each child table once with a WHERE item_id IN (...) or unfiltered join, then lint in memory.",
  "legacy": {
